            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prithvi Pai",
                        "email": "prithvi24pai@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PrithviPai24"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for this infra. \nBased on this I was able to develop oem/nvidia."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 278,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "How do we ensure they all get compiled in CI?  Do you want them as a list like this or do you want them as individual features?\n\nI guess it looks like `libpldm` made it an array where all of them are included by default in the `value`.\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/libpldm/blob/ffdc405cd8517f4c090f78e0f7692a877b0c75b6/meson.options#L17\n\npldm did it as separate meson.options:\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/pldm/blob/master/meson.options#L158"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 278,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "After I pushed this and had the discussion on discord, I was thinking I might add two more options to the list of choices: 'none', and 'all', with the default value set to 'all'"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.options",
                    "line": 278,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "\ud83d\udc4d"
                },
                {
                    "file": "oem/example/meson.build",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "You might want this as a variable elsewhere."
                },
                {
                    "file": "oem/example/meson.build",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "If I recall correctly, the providers libraries need this. I should probably dig into why."
                },
                {
                    "file": "oem/example/meson.build",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah, all I meant was do something like `override_options: ipmi_plugin_options,` so we don't have these weird `ld` flags sprinkled everywhere but it is somewhat self-documenting.\n\nI think the `b_lundef` is to allow the library to link against symbols that don't exist, because `main` provides them.  That's how you have to link plugins."
                }
            ],
